  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first of six runs: 14 witnesses, 19 names, no compositions, and one narrowing I declared.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_257_1_o1.lean`):\n- **When it applies:** at the moment the subject vehicle enters an intersection X, having been on an approach lane c into X at the previous observation, while a stop or yield sign governs c or X. It does not apply if a police officer, or a traffic signal that is working, governs c or X.\n- **What it requires:** looking back from the entry, an observation where the subject was on c inside the stopping zone. At a stop sign that means a complete halt; with only a yield sign, a speed at or below `p.yield_line_speed_max`. The zone is set by the first that exists: the stop line marking c, then the crosswalk marking c, then the edge of X.\n- **How far back it looks:** the search ends at the last observation where the subject was upstream of the zone, or at its earlier exit from X, whichever is later. If the recording starts before either is reached, the result is unknown.\n\n**One departure from the blueprint**, declared as a narrowing on span e: the blueprint ends the search at the subject's previous entry into X, but I end it at the subject's exit from X after that entry. The formula language can't tell the entry being judged apart from an earlier entry into the same intersection, so a search bounded at \"an entry\" would stop at the current one. The only effect is that a stop made while the vehicle still overlaps X after an earlier entry doesn't count for the next entry.\n\n**The witnesses:** the eight planned scenarios, plus six I added so every part of the formula changes some verdict:\n- **branch_4 and branch_5:** the crosswalk case, compliant and violated.\n- **branch_6 and branch_7:** the intersection-edge case, compliant and violated.\n- **branch_8:** a dark signal governs c, so the rule still applies.\n- **branch_9:** the vehicle backs out of X and re-enters without stopping again.\n\n`forbid` uses a rolling pass at 3 m/s through the stop line's zone.\n\nThe full record, including the smaller reading choices, is in `task_result.md`.",
